From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:23:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pdu,graphics): decode ClearCodec residual, subcodec and
 RLEX data one item at a time

The ClearCodec decoder painted its bands layer one V-bar at a time, but
still collected the rest of a stream before painting it: every segment
of the residual layer (eight bytes, for as few as four on the wire),
every region of the subcodec layer (20 bytes in the WebAssembly build,
32 on 64-bit, for a 13-byte header), and every segment of an RLEX
region (eight bytes, for one or two). The vectors grew by doubling, and
infallibly. On 64-bit, a 64 MiB residual layer took 384 MiB and a
64 MiB subcodec layer 192 MiB. A layer can be 256 MiB, the most ZGFX
lets one PDU decompress to, and an 8192x8192 RLEX region can carry
192 MiB of one-byte segments: in the WebAssembly build, a command of
such a region trapped a fresh instance, the one every session shares,
after growing it to 2.9 GiB, its vector of segments short of the 2 GiB
it was growing to.

ironrdp-pdu's new decode_residual_layer_segments,
decode_subcodec_layer_regions and decode_rlex_segments iterate over a
residual layer's segments, a subcodec layer's regions and an RLEX
region's segments (after its palette, of at most 127 entries), decoding
one at a time, and the ClearCodec decoder paints each as it comes: the
layers above now take no memory besides the image, and that RLEX
command grows a fresh instance to 1 GiB, for itself, the copies ZGFX
and the PDU decoder make of it, and the 256 MiB image. A stream fails
where it failed before: the segments past a full image are still read,
so a malformed one still fails it. decode_residual_layer,
decode_subcodec_layer and decode_rlex still collect.
